To perform repetitive energy minimizations as one specified 
dihedral angle is varied from 0 to 360 degrees-

The input Z-matrix is dihzmat

FOR OPTIMIZATIONS with OPLS-AA:
Consult the dihcmd file for specification of the dihedral angle
to be varied and the increment between minimizations. Note that the
chosen dihedral must be moved from the list of variable dihedral
angles to the list of additional dihedral angles in the Z-matrix.
Thus, dihedral angle 6 is listed as an additional one in example dihzmat.

Execute under UNIX/Linux via:
csh dihcmd 

The results are in the dih.CSV and dihout files.
The results can be displayed with the perl script, dihxmgr:
dihxmgr dih.CSV plt
xmgr plt

or by input of the dih.CSV file into Excel, gnumeric, etc.

