FOR OPTIMIZATIONS with GB/SA, AM1, PM3 or PDDG/PM3:
Use the dihGBcmd, dihAM1cmd, dihPM3cmd, or dihPDGcmd command files
in the same manner. You can use the same dihzmat as above,
and edit the cmd file to specify the driver dihedral and increment.
The output is in dihAM1.CSV, dihAM1out, etc.
The molecule is expected to be uncharged and a singlet in these
cases. If this is not true, you need to modify the cmd file
to use the appropriate par file from the scripts directory.
